  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Eastern Air Express obligated $224M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Eastern Air Express received 61 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.7M and obligations up 3870.1% year over year. Eastern Air Express saw most obligations come from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $216M. Eastern Air Express also received obligations from the Department of Defense and the Department of the Interior, at $5.6M and $3M respectively. Eastern Air Express obligations were small in earlier years, ranging from $0 in FY21 to $5.6M in FY25, before this year’s large increase. Current-year totals are partial because the period covered is fiscal year to date, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables represent total contract values rather than current-year obligations.",
